2... c5 3. d5 { Pushes past the c5 pawn and gains space. The pawn on d5 cramps Black's pieces and cannot easily be attacked. } 3... exd5 ( 3... Nf6 4. Nc3 { Develops and protects the e4 pawn, which Black's knight attacks. } 4... d6 ( 4... exd5 $2 5. e5 $1 { Hits the knight, which has no good square, and Black's d5 pawn will fall. } 5... Ng8 6. Qxd5 ) 5. dxe6 { Takes the pawn so Black cannot keep the closed centre it wants. } 5... Bxe6 6. Nge2 ) ( 3... d6 4. Nc3 { Develops and guards e4. } 4... Nf6 { The same position as 3...Nf6 4.Nc3 d6, where White takes on e6. } ) ( 3... e5 { Locks the centre. Black's dark-squared bishop and the knights now have few good squares. } 4. Nc3 { Develops. With the centre closed White has time; the knight can later go to b5 or reroute. } 4... d6 5. Nf3 Be7 6. Bd3 { Plan: castle, then a4 to stop ...b5, and Nd2-c4 to put a knight on a strong square. White has more space on both wings. } ) 4. exd5 d6 ( 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { Develops and guards the d5 pawn. } 5... d6 { The same position as 4...d6 5.Nc3 Nf6. } ) 5. Nc3 { Develops and guards d5. The open e-file is what Black needs to fight for. } 5... Nf6 6. Bd3 { The bishop eyes the kingside and protects the pawn on e4 if needed. } 6... Be7 7. Nge2 { Develops without blocking the f-pawn and heads for g3. } 7... O-O 8. O-O { Plan: finish castling, bring the knight to g3 and play a4 and Bf4. Black's bishop on c8 has few good squares, and White's is free. } *
